<title>UK: POLL - Forecasts for Oct 30 UK monetary meeting.</title>
<headline>POLL - Forecasts for Oct 30 UK monetary meeting.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters' polled 20 economists ahead of Wednesday's UK monthly monetary meeting. The economists, surveyed on Monday answered the following questions. 1. Will the Chancellor change interest rates at the next meeting on October 30? 2. If No, will he raise or cut interest rates and by how much? 3a. When rates next change, will they move up or down and by how much? 4. At what levels will rates peak in 1997?</p>
<p>The results are detailed below:</p>
<p> Average		 1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p> BankAmerica	   1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 25bp   4. 6.25</p>
<p> Charterhouse	  1. Yes 2. Oct 30 3. Up 50bp   4. 8.50</p>
<p> CS First Boston     1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p> Deutsche Morg Gren  1. No  2. Q197   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.25</p>
<p> DKB		     1. No  2. Q397   3. Up 50bp   4. 6.25</p>
<p> HSBC James Capel    1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 25bp   4. 6.75</p>
<p> Kleinwort Benson    1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 6.50</p>
<p> Lehman Brothers     1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.25</p>
<p> Lloyds TSB Group    1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 6.75</p>
<p> London Bond Broking 1. No  2. Q496   3. Down 25bp 4. 6.75</p>
<p> Morgan Stanley	1. No  2. Q197   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.75</p>
<p> Natwest Group	 1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.25</p>
<p> Nikko Europe	  1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 25bp   4. 6.25</p>
<p> Paine Webber	  1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 25pb   4. 6.75</p>
<p> Panmure Gordon	1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p> Societe Generale    1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p> Standard Chartered  1. No  2. Q197   3. Up 25bp   4. 6.75</p>
<p> UBS		     1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 25bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p> Union Discount	1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 50bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p> Yamaichi		1. No  2. Q297   3. Up 25bp   4. 7.00</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7958.</p>
